/target

# musl release builds
/target-musl

# Renders made while working in the checkout.
#
# `--out` defaults to `image.png` for generate/edit and `video.mp4` for video, so
# running either from the repository root drops the result straight into the
# working tree — where `git add -A` picks it up like anything else. That is not
# hypothetical: a 4.9 MB test render rode into `d37737c` exactly this way and
# would have shipped as a tenth of the published crate.
#
# Anchored to the root, so a deliberate fixture in a subdirectory is unaffected.
/image.png
/video.mp4

# ...and the batch forms, `--count N` writing image-1.png, image-2.png, ...
/image-*.png
/video-*.mp4
